From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MYIR Tech <support@myirtech.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 17:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: myir: enable CRYP1 without DMA

The OP-TEE RIFSC configuration assigns CRYP1 to the non-secure world,
while CRYP2 remains secure and restricted to CID2. Enable only CRYP1
for Linux on the MYIR STM32MP257 board family.

CRYP1 DMA transfers currently raise an HPDMA data transfer error and a
SERC illegal-access event on this platform. The STM32 CRYP driver already
supports an interrupt-driven fallback when no DMA channels are described,
so remove the DMA properties until the HPDMA path is fixed. Encryption is
still performed by the CRYP hardware.

Signed-off-by: MYIR Tech <support@myirtech.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/myir/myb-stm32mp257x-base.dtsi | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/myir/myb-stm32mp257x-base.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/myir/myb-stm32mp257x-base.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/myir/myb-stm32mp257x-base.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/myir/myb-stm32mp257x-base.dtsi
@@ -694,6 +694,12 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&cryp1 {
+	/delete-property/ dmas;
+	/delete-property/ dma-names;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &cs_cpu_debug0 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
